  clock: 5  # 38b8
  nonce: 38b8  # 38b8
  message: "SATISFIED. Fixed in PR #2274 (dev 769b52eec): .githooks/repair-agent-perms.sh repairs only .agent/tracker and .agent/tracker-workspace (an empty list returns, so find never searches the current directory). Owner-approved governance change (2026-11-18), merged by auto-pr without --gov.\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE. (1) Production-path test: tests/test_transcript_perms.py::TestGitHooksKeepTranscriptsOwnerOnly drives the REAL post-checkout and post-merge hooks through a real branch checkout and a real merge in a throwaway repository (a fake `id` reports another primary group so the two-user branch fires): a 600 transcript and 700 archive dirs stay so; both tracker trees still get g+rw / g+rwxs. Red before the fix (transcript 0660). Mutations kosok/muts.tsv: 4 of 4 red. (2) The item's own repro on this checkout, 2026-11-19 ~06:40Z, after tightening the files earlier checkouts had loosened (once, with transcript_perms.sh's harden helpers): stat -> 600 .last_session_transcript.jsonl, 600 .training-data.jsonl, 700 .archived-transcripts; `git checkout -- .ci/affected-tests.txt` -> same; `git checkout -b tmp/kosok-check && git checkout dev` -> same; 0 of the top-level transcript files and 0 of 720 archive/rotation-queue/deprecated-datasets entries carry a group or other bit; .agent/tracker and tracker/.ops stay drwxrwsr-x project-dev. A live merge was not exercised (origin/dev had nothing to merge); the hook-driven test covers it.\nNOT DECIDED HERE (owner's call, not asked again): whether INV-todig is reopened."  # 38b8
